userStories.description:
**Goal** — The runner parses the status.json `workflow` block and nax's `result.json`, judges a workflow RUN from the workflow outcome, and falls back to the workflow PR url for `resultPrUrl`.

**Motivation** — runVerdict returns COMPLETED for `run.status === 'completed'` with no `postRun.finish`, but nax writes `run.status: "completed"` even when the workflow ends as a draft (nax#2508), so a draft run reads as COMPLETED and no human is told; `resultPrUrl` comes only from `postRun.finish.url`, so the job never gets nax's PR link.

**Approach**
Rulings: R1 a `draft` outcome maps to ESCALATED (existing needs-a-human state and notification); `ready` -> COMPLETED; `local-only`, or a `workflow` block with no outcome -> FAILED. R2 koda adds no profile injection or toggle; it reads workflow output whenever nax produces it and keeps today's behaviour when it does not. D1: nax's status.json `run.id` (e.g. `run-cb319c9d-2026-10-13T15-08-43.285`) is NOT the workflow run id that names the `workflow/<id>/` directory (runtime UUID, e.g. `fab5b9af-d3a3-41f2-91ed-62372a733c03`). The runner detects a workflow run from the status.json `workflow` block, never from a path built from `naxRunId`, and locates `result.json` as the newest regular file `workflow/*/result.json` whose modification time is at or after the job row's `createdAt`. D4: the server keeps at most 500 characters of a runner state reason, so the runner clips the whole workflow reason, prefix included, to 500 characters.

nax input `status.json` (present only in workflow mode):
```json
{ "run": { "id": "run-cb319c9d-2026-10-13T15-08-43.285", "status": "completed" },
  "workflow": { "step": "done", "stories": { "US-001": { "state": "complete", "round": 1 } },
                "outcome": "draft", "url": "https://github.com/nathapp-io/koda/pull/269" } }
```
nax input `result.json` (`schemaVersion: 1`); `verdict` is absent until the feature workflow publishes:
```json
{ "schemaVersion": 1, "runId": "fab5b9af-d3a3-41f2-91ed-62372a733c03", "feature": "fleet-s5a-thread-handoff",
  "stories": {},
  "verdict": { "workflowPassed": true, "outcome": "draft", "reasons": ["CI failed: test"], "openItems": [] } }
```
`FeatureOutcome` is `ready | draft | local-only`.

`StatusView` (apps/runner/src/verdict/status-view.ts): baseline `{ run, progress?, cost?, current?, lastHeartbeat?, updatedAt?, postRun? }`, `parseStatusView` drops `workflow`. Target adds `readonly workflow?: WorkflowView`. `parseStatusView` sets it only when `raw.workflow` is an object with a string `step`; an `outcome` outside the three values is dropped (absent); `url` is kept only when it starts with `https://`.

`runVerdict` (apps/runner/src/verdict/run-verdict.ts): baseline `runVerdict(input: { cancelRequested: boolean; status: StatusView | null }): Verdict`. Target adds optional `workflowReasons`. Rows in order: cancel -> CANCELLED; no status -> FAILED `no status.json`; **`status.workflow` present** -> the workflow table below; otherwise today's finish rows unchanged.

Workflow rows (reasons = `workflowReasons` joined with `; `; the whole reason, prefix included, is clipped to 500 characters):
| `status.workflow` | Verdict state | Reason |
|---|---|---|
| `outcome: 'ready'` | COMPLETED | null |
| `outcome: 'draft'` | ESCALATED | `workflow draft: <reasons>`, or `workflow draft` when there are no reasons |
| `outcome: 'local-only'` | FAILED | `workflow local-only: <reasons>`, or `workflow local-only` |
| no `outcome` | FAILED | `workflow ended at step <step>` |

`run.status` and `postRun` are not consulted for a workflow run. The reason prefixes never start with the budget-stop text the web page parses (`budgetStopPolicyId`).

`findWorkflowResult` lists `workflow/` with `readdir(..., { withFileTypes: true })` and keeps only real directories (a symlinked directory is skipped), checks each `result.json` with `lstat` (only a regular file of at most 1 MiB is read; a symlink is skipped), orders the candidates by mtime newest first, and returns the first that `parseWorkflowResult` accepts. nax writes `result.json` before the verdict exists, so a newer verdict-less file is passed over for an older one that has a verdict. Non-string reasons are dropped.

`mapStatusToSnapshot` (apps/runner/src/watcher/status-snapshot.ts): baseline `resultPrUrl` = `status.postRun?.finish?.url`; target `status.postRun?.finish?.url ?? status.workflow?.url`.

**Scope** — In: StatusView.workflow and parsing, workflow-result.ts, workflow rows of runVerdict, snapshot resultPrUrl fallback. Out: JobExecutor/HostExecutor/FakeExecutor methods and JobRun changes (US-002), the stash and bundle (US-003), any API/web work. PLAN jobs unchanged. Existing finish-row verdict tests stay unchanged.

**Interface**
```ts
// apps/runner/src/verdict/status-view.ts
interface WorkflowView { readonly step: string; readonly outcome?: 'ready' | 'draft' | 'local-only'; readonly url?: string }
// StatusView gains: readonly workflow?: WorkflowView

// apps/runner/src/verdict/run-verdict.ts
runVerdict(input: { cancelRequested: boolean; status: StatusView | null; workflowReasons?: readonly string[] }): Verdict

// apps/runner/src/verdict/workflow-result.ts (new)
export interface WorkflowResult {
  readonly runId: string;
  readonly outcome: 'ready' | 'draft' | 'local-only';
  readonly reasons: readonly string[];   // at most 20, each at most 500 characters
}
/** null unless raw is a schemaVersion 1 result with a verdict whose outcome is one of the three values. */
export function parseWorkflowResult(raw: unknown): WorkflowResult | null;
/** Newest-first over `<featureDir>/workflow/<id>/result.json` (real directories, regular files, at most 1 MiB, mtime >= sinceMs): the first that parses, with its run dir. */
export async function findWorkflowResult(featureDir: string, sinceMs: number): Promise<{ result: WorkflowResult; runDir: string } | null>;
```

**Goal** — The fleet job page renders the workflow outcome, reasons and open items from the job's `workflow` field.

**Motivation** — Reasons and open items are otherwise lost, so a human cannot see why a workflow run ended as a draft.

**Approach**
The wire shape from the API (US-004) is `{ runId, outcome, workflowPassed, reasons: string[], openItems: { id, kind, issue, severity|null, file|null, line|null, suggestion|null }[] }`. `FleetJobDto` (apps/web/lib/fleet-types.ts): add `workflow: FleetJobWorkflowDto | null`, with web types `FleetJobWorkflowDto` and `FleetJobWorkflowItemDto` mirroring the API DTO.

New component `apps/web/components/fleet/FleetJobWorkflow.vue` (prop `workflow: FleetJobWorkflowDto`), rendered by the job page `apps/web/pages/[project]/fleet/jobs/[id]/index.vue` below the state row when `job.workflow` is non-null:
- outcome badge `data-testid="fleet-job-workflow-outcome"` with the text of `fleet.jobs.workflow.outcome.<ready|draft|localOnly>`;
- reasons list `data-testid="fleet-job-workflow-reasons"` (one `li` per reason), hidden when there are none;
- open items list `data-testid="fleet-job-workflow-open-items"`: one row per item showing `kind`, `severity` when present, `file:line` when `file` is present (`file` alone when `line` is null), and `issue`; hidden when empty.

The page imports `~/components/fleet/FleetJobWorkflow.vue` explicitly, as it does every sibling component (the test mount helper has no Nuxt auto-import); the component is also added to `FLEET_COMPONENT_FILES` in `apps/web/tests/helpers/mount-sfc.ts`. The page-level tests follow `fleet-job-logs-page.spec.ts`: they alias `~/composables/useApi`, `~/composables/useFleetApprovals`, `~/components/fleet/JobAnalytics.vue` and `~/components/fleet/config/ConfigPrDialog.vue` to stubs, provide the page's remaining composables (`useRoute`, `useI18n`, `useAppToast`, `useAuth`, `useFleetJobs`, `useFleetDispatchOptions`, `useProjectMemberNames`, `useFleetRepoConfig`, `useProjectViewerRole`, `useFleetJobLogs`, `useProjectEvents`) as globals, and load a full `FleetJobDto` fixture.

i18n keys in `apps/web/i18n/locales/en.json` and `zh.json` (parity is enforced by the existing `tests/i18n/fleet-locale-parity.spec.ts` and `used-keys-exist.spec.ts`): `fleet.jobs.workflow.title`, `fleet.jobs.workflow.outcome.ready`, `.draft`, `.localOnly`, `fleet.jobs.workflow.reasons`, `fleet.jobs.workflow.openItems`. No new API calls: the page already loads the job with `GET` by id. Web strings live only in web i18n files (not API i18n); the web uses Nuxt-native composables, no generated client.

**Scope** — In: FleetJobDto type additions, FleetJobWorkflow.vue, page wiring, mount-sfc registration, en/zh i18n keys. Out: API column/DTO (US-004), the C3 thread page (reuses this component later), any new API call.

**Interface**
```ts
// apps/web/lib/fleet-types.ts
export interface FleetJobWorkflowItemDto { id: string; kind: string; issue: string; severity: string | null; file: string | null; line: number | null; suggestion: string | null }
export interface FleetJobWorkflowDto { runId: string; outcome: 'ready' | 'draft' | 'local-only'; workflowPassed: boolean; reasons: string[]; openItems: FleetJobWorkflowItemDto[] }
// FleetJobDto gains: workflow: FleetJobWorkflowDto | null
```
